# 📘 Day 07 – 8051 Microcontroller Basics

Welcome to **Day 07** of my **Embedded Firmware Engineer Roadmap**.

Today I started learning the **8051 Microcontroller**, the foundation of Embedded Systems programming. I explored its architecture, memory organization, pin configuration, Special Function Registers (SFRs), clock and reset circuits, and learned how to write and simulate my first Embedded C programs using **Keil μVision** and **Proteus**.

---

## 🎯 Goal

- Understand the fundamentals of Embedded Systems.
- Learn the basics of Microcontrollers.
- Study the architecture and features of the 8051 Microcontroller.
- Understand the 8051 pin diagram and memory organization.
- Learn Special Function Registers (SFRs).
- Understand clock, reset, and machine cycle concepts.
- Set up the Embedded C development environment.
- Write and simulate simple GPIO programs.

